@page "/projects/blazor-app/azure"
@page "/projects/game-development/background"

<div class="project-page page-content">
	<header class="project-header">
		<p class="eyebrow">Game Development</p>
		<h1>Background</h1>
		<p class="tagline">The game side of my work sits on top of a formal game design education and a professional engineering career.</p>
	</header>

	<section class="project-section">
		<h2>Education</h2>
		<p>
			I graduated from Kennesaw State University in January 2019 with a Bachelor of Science in Computer Game Design and Development. That program gave me a foundation in game systems, interactive design, production thinking, and the practical constraints that come with building playable work.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="project-section">
		<h2>College Portfolio Work</h2>
		<p>
			I have additional game portfolio projects from my college days. Those projects show the early side of the craft: learning systems, building prototypes, exploring mechanics, and developing the habits that later carried into production software.
		</p>
		<p>
			I am keeping this section focused on the through-line rather than listing every older project: KSU gave me the game-development foundation, Infiniroller shows independent release experience, and Versus With Verses shows the current blend of Unity, APIs, and Azure.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="project-section">
		<h2>Professional Carryover</h2>
		<ul class="project-list">
			<li>C# fluency from both Unity and professional .NET development.</li>
			<li>Backend architecture habits applied to game-adjacent services.</li>
			<li>API integration experience from web systems brought into Unity workflows.</li>
			<li>Azure deployment and configuration practices used to support active game projects.</li>
			<li>Independent delivery discipline from shipping both software and creative work.</li>
		</ul>
	</section>
</div>
